        "citations": null,
        "text": "I'll analyze the California statute carefully. Key observations:\n\n- §86113: Lobbyists prepare a periodic report, but provide it to their employer/firm (not file separately with SOS)\n- §86114: Lobbying FIRMS file periodic reports (which include the lobbyist's verified report under (a)(4))\n- §86116: Lobbyist EMPLOYERS file periodic reports (which include the lobbyist's verified report under (e))\n- §86117: Reports filed quarterly\n- §86118: Filed with Secretary of State\n\nSo lobbyists themselves do NOT file a separate spending report with the state — they provide it to their firm/employer, which then files. This is critical for the \"is the lobbyist the named filer\" qualifier on most rows.\n\nHowever, §86113 does require the lobbyist to \"complete and verify a periodic report\" — there is a lobbyist-specific report, even though it's transmitted via the firm/employer. I'll interpret the strict qualifier as making most rows FALSE since the filer with the state is the firm/employer, not the lobbyist.",
